UnitToken::constructor
├── when minter is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when voting escrow is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when migration is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when Velodrome migration is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the migration opening timestamp is not week aligned
│   └── it should revert with InvalidMigrationOpen
├── when the migration opening timestamp is not in the future
│   └── it should revert with InvalidMigrationOpen
└── when parameters are valid
    ├── it should set the MINTER immutable to _minter
    ├── it should set the VOTING_ESCROW immutable to _votingEscrow
    ├── it should set the MIGRATION immutable to _migration
    ├── it should set the VELODROME_MIGRATION immutable to _velodromeMigration
    ├── it should set TRANSFERS_ENABLED_AT to one week after _migrationOpen
    ├── it should set the name to _name
    ├── it should set the symbol to _symbol
    ├── it should set the name hash to a hash of _name bytes
    ├── it should mint _migrationAllocation to _migration
    ├── it should mint _velodromeAllocation to _velodromeMigration
    ├── it should set total supply to the sum of both migration allocations
    ├── it should emit Transfer for the migration allocation
    └── it should emit Transfer for the Velodrome migration allocation

UnitToken::mint
├── when caller is not minter
│   └── it should revert with NotMinter
├── when caller is minter and recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when caller is minter and total supply overflows
│   └── it should revert with TotalSupplyOverflow
└── when caller is minter and recipient is valid
    ├── it should mint tokens to the recipient
    ├── it should increase total supply by the amount
    └── it should emit Transfer with address(0), _recipient, _amount

UnitToken::burn
├── when caller is not an authorized burner
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotBurner
├── when voting escrow has insufficient balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance
├── when voting escrow has enough balance
│   ├── it should burn tokens from voting escrow
│   ├── it should decrease total supply by the amount
│   └── it should emit Transfer with _VOTING_ESCROW, address(0), _amount
├── when migration has insufficient balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance
├── when migration has enough balance
│   ├── it should burn tokens from migration
│   ├── it should decrease total supply by the amount
│   └── it should emit Transfer with _MIGRATION, address(0), _amount
├── when Velodrome migration has insufficient balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance
└── when Velodrome migration has enough balance
    ├── it should burn tokens from Velodrome migration
    ├── it should decrease total supply by the amount
    └── it should emit Transfer with _VELODROME_MIGRATION, address(0), _amount

UnitToken::transfer
├── when transfers are disabled and caller is not a migration sender
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when transfers are disabled and caller is migration
│   └── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
├── when transfers are disabled and caller is Velodrome migration
│   └── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
├── when transfers are disabled and only the recipient is migration
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when transfers are disabled and only the recipient is Velodrome migration
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when transfers are disabled and recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when current timestamp equals the transfer activation timestamp
│   └── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
├── when recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when caller has insufficient balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance
├── when caller has enough balance
│   ├── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
│   ├── it should keep total supply unchanged
│   └── it should emit Transfer with _caller, _recipient, _amount
└── when recipient is caller
    ├── it should keep the caller balance unchanged
    ├── it should keep total supply unchanged
    └── it should emit Transfer with _caller, _caller, _amount

UnitToken::transferFrom
├── when transfers are disabled and from is not a migration sender
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when transfers are disabled and from is migration
│   └── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
├── when transfers are disabled and from is Velodrome migration
│   └── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
├── when transfers are disabled and only the caller is migration
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when transfers are disabled and only the recipient is migration
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when transfers are disabled and recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert with TransfersDisabled
├── when current timestamp equals the transfer activation timestamp
│   └── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
├── when recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when from address has insufficient balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance
├── when caller has insufficient allowance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientAllowance
├── when caller is PermitTwo and no approval has been given
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientAllowance
├── when caller has finite allowance
│   ├── when finite allowance recipient is not from
│   │   ├── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
│   │   ├── it should decrease the caller allowance
│   │   ├── it should keep total supply unchanged
│   │   └── it should emit Transfer with _from, _recipient, _amount
│   └── when finite allowance recipient is from
│       ├── it should keep the from balance unchanged
│       ├── it should decrease the caller allowance
│       ├── it should keep total supply unchanged
│       └── it should emit Transfer with _from, _from, _amount
└── when caller has infinite allowance
    ├── when infinite allowance recipient is not from
    │   ├── it should transfer tokens to the recipient
    │   ├── it should keep the caller allowance unchanged
    │   ├── it should keep total supply unchanged
    │   └── it should emit Transfer with _from, _recipient, _amount
    └── when infinite allowance recipient is from
        ├── it should keep the from balance unchanged
        ├── it should keep the caller allowance unchanged
        ├── it should keep total supply unchanged
        └── it should emit Transfer with _from, _from, _amount

UnitToken::approve
├── when called
│   ├── it should approve the spender
│   └── it should emit Approval with _owner, _spender, _amount
└── when spender is PermitTwo
    ├── it should approve PermitTwo
    └── it should emit Approval with _owner, PermitTwo, _amount

UnitToken::allowance
├── when spender is PermitTwo and no approval has been given
│   └── it should return zero
├── when spender is PermitTwo and approval has been given
│   └── it should return its allowance
├── when spender is any non PermitTwo address and no approval has been given
│   └── it should return zero
└── when spender is any non PermitTwo address and approval has been given
    └── it should return its allowance

UnitToken::permit
├── when deadline has expired
│   └── it should revert with PermitExpired
├── when signature is invalid
│   └── it should revert with InvalidPermit
├── when signature is replayed
│   └── it should revert with InvalidPermit
├── when spender is PermitTwo and signature is valid
│   ├── it should approve PermitTwo
│   ├── it should increment the owner nonce
│   └── it should emit Approval with _permitOwner, PermitTwo, _amount
└── when spender is not PermitTwo and signature is valid
    ├── it should approve the spender
    ├── it should increment the owner nonce
    └── it should emit Approval with _permitOwner, _spender, _amount

UnitToken::DOMAIN_SEPARATOR
└── when called
    └── it should return the expected domain separator

UnitToken::name
└── when called
    └── it should return the token name

UnitToken::symbol
└── when called
    └── it should return the token symbol
